    <item>
      <title>Squeak 2.35.5</title>
      <pubDate>Sat, 28 Nov 2026 06:56:13 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>23505</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.35.5</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><p><strong>Invitations that just work.</strong></p><ul><li>Join never says "already used": joining twice, or a Pond you're already in, simply opens it.</li><li>Invitations to you appear and disappear within seconds. If the list can't refresh, it says so with Try again.</li><li>Inviting several people is one quick step: each address shows Inviting…, then Invited or the reason. An email that didn't arrive shows Resend.</li><li>Invitations show who invited you by name, never "Someone".</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.35.4</h4><p><strong>The Room speaks plainly.</strong></p><ul><li>Ducks write in the Room for teammates who aren't engineers: what changed, whether it's ready to try, and what you need to do. Commit codes, file names and test counts stay in the Duck's own chat.</li><li>When a Duck asks you a question, it shows in the Room too, with its options as buttons. Answer there or in the chat.</li><li>No more "Claude" tags or email addresses in the Room: Ducks and people show by name.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.35.3</h4><p><strong>Ducks are Open or Closed.</strong></p><ul><li>"Off duty" is now Closed and "On duty" is now Open, everywhere: the roster, the Dashboard, search and the @ list. A closed Duck says "Closed 3d ago" and has Reopen.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
